round 52 (update): 4/4 members, 3 ideas forecast; scored E046; COUNTEREXAMPLE E046 outside every range (time)
H1.3.6->refuted, H1.2.3->retired, H2.2.4->supported, H2.4->retired, H2.6.8->inconclusive, H4.3.1->refuted, H6.1->refuted, H6.1.1->refuted, H6.3->supported, +H4.1.5, +H4.1.6, +H4.4.2, +H4.2.6, +H2.6.9, +H6.5, +H6.5.1, +H6.6, +H6.6.1, +H1.7, +H1.7.1, +H1.5.9. Revised the tree after E043–E046, the search results and the review. Bookkeeping: H1.3.6 refuted (E044's paired test found no effect from BN recalibration), and the BN-mixture caveat was dropped from H1.3. H4.3.1 refuted, since three builds of the same E036 commit gave seeds 0–2 means of 0.7532, 0.7525 and 0.7497. H4.1 rewritten to cover the 0.35 pp rebuild spread, the persistent seed-1 deficit (probably tied to init) and the open question of winner's curse vs seed-set difficulty. H4 and H1 headlines restated: the unselected population is ~0.7535, local pass probability is ≤50%, and there is one fixed keep gate. H1 confidence lowered, since no accuracy-per-epoch booster has held up since E016. E043 settles H2.2.4 by calculation (conv kernels run well above 90 TFLOP/s), refutes H6.1/H6.1.1 (24 px step time is pixel-proportional), supports H6.3, and caps Muon levers at ~2.5% of a step (H1.2.3 retired, H1.2.2 re-scoped). Search lowers H6.4/H6.4.2 (Cin=24 is already tensor-core aligned) and bears on H1.5.4 (the reference renormalizes filters) and on H4.3 (PCIe specs). H2.3.8's invalid cross-seed comparison was withdrawn. E045's rate was corrected to ~1.5 s/pp, the same as the dial. H4.2's dial slope was flagged as stale. H2.6.8 marked inconclusive. H2.4 retired. New items: build reproducibility (H4.1.5), seed-1 init diagnostic (H4.1.6), winner's-curse vs seed-set test (H4.4.2), dial re-measure and margin top-up on the tip (H4.2.6), a decisive same-build test for the group-2 freeze plus top-up (H2.6.9), the memory-bound elementwise share with a GELU→ReLU test (H6.5/H6.5.1), and truncation saving 1.5–2× its FLOP share, which explains the E028/E046 counterexamples (H6.6/H6.6.1). Also new: capacity moved to group 3 (H1.7/H1.7.1) and ghost BN (H1.5.9). The other counterexamples are accounted for: E043's accuracy by rebuild noise, E030/E032 by the averaging local optimum in H1.3, and E031's time by its uncertain base (H2.7). Recommended next steps: make builds reproducible (H4.1.5), then buy margin (H4.2.6), then run cuts against same-build baselines on seeds 13–32.
added I074, I075, I076, I077, I078; dropped I073. The tip (E036, 5.31 s) has an unselected 20-seed mean of about 0.7535 and clears the local 0.753 bar on only some builds. So the H4 gate makes buying margin the top priority. I074 (H4.2.6, priority 5) re-prices the post-freeze epoch dial: +0.25 epoch, judged on seeds 13–32 against a fresh E036 baseline from the same build session. Later ideas reuse that baseline. I075 (H2.6.9, priority 4) is the decisive test of the committee's shared E046 crux: the group-2 freeze plus a 0.25-epoch top-up, run in the same session. It should dominate E036 (about −2% time at equal accuracy) if group 2's freeze cost holds at −0.14 pp. I076 (H2.2, priority 3) goes after the 2.5% of non-step GPU work (copies, interpolate, gathers) that E047 found, with identical math. I077 (H1.7, priority 3, explore) adds a cheap Dirac-initialized fourth conv to group 3 at 3×3 maps. It tests whether late capacity is the structural sample-efficiency lever H1 says is the only remaining one. I078 (H6.5.1, priority 2, explore) swaps GELU for ReLU to test whether the 27% memory-bound share depends on the activation type. I073 is dropped because E047 refuted its premise (conv1 is 6–9% of a step, below the 10% bar). I072 (loss-based selection) is still running. Queue: 5 new ideas plus 1 running, about 2/3 exploit.
